To create a C++ function that converts Markdown formatted text to HTML, you can use a markdown library like libMarkdown. Here's a simple function that takes a reference to a `std::string` containing Markdown text and returns a `std::string` containing HTML formatted text:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <markdown.h>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    markdown::Markdown md;
    std::string html = md.convert(markdown);
    return html;
}

int main() {
    std::string markdown = "# Hello, Markdown!\nThis is a test.";
    std::string html = markdownToHtml(markdown);
    std::cout << "Markdown: " << markdown << std::endl;
    std::cout << "HTML: " << html << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This function uses the `markdown::Markdown` class to convert the Markdown text to HTML. You may need to include the `markdown.h` header and link against the `markdown` library in your project.

